"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_langmaterial\",\"type\":\"langmaterial\",\"content\":[\"English, Spanish; Castilian.\"],\"persistent_id\":\"be6e5c8078b8a7712a211269e2765831\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:21:29','2022-04-09 23:21:29','2022-04-09 23:21:29',NULL,NULL,590,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(871,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_langmaterial\",\"type\":\"langmaterial\",\"content\":[\"English.\"],\"persistent_id\":\"6804277e0880a4aebd246b35a56d930b\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:21:29','2022-04-09 23:21:29','2022-04-09 23:21:29',NULL,NULL,595,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(872,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_langmaterial\",\"type\":\"langmaterial\",\"content\":[\"English, Spanish; Castilian.\"],\"persistent_id\":\"a85c7049c07f32ffa8b536a84c45d9c9\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:21:29','2022-04-09 23:21:29','2022-04-09 23:21:29',NULL,NULL,598,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(873,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_langmaterial\",\"type\":\"langmaterial\",\"content\":[\"English, Spanish; Castilian.\"],\"persistent_id\":\"73e8447134fb1b26db7ed9512dbaee77\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:21:29','2022-04-09 23:21:29','2022-04-09 23:21:29',NULL,NULL,601,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(878,1,NULL,4535,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Microfilm original. Accesso limitado a empleados de Special Collections.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"4a14bf5f828e58d2522270c66cfed9e7\"}],\"type\":\"accessrestrict\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_e785ee459160669c8e8403b897a78339\",\"label\":\"Conditions Governing Access\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:21:31','2022-04-09 23:21:31','2022-04-09 23:21:31',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(891,1,NULL,4539,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The <title>American Popular Revolutionary Alliance Party (APRA)</title> series, 1930-1991 (0.66 linear feet) includes correspondence, publications, and propaganda produced by APRA leadership. The correspondence located in Box 1 is arranged in chronological order, while the additional material in Box 12 is arranged alphabetically. This series chiefly consists of official correspondence from APRA leadership to Luis Alberto Sánchez or to party members as a whole. Luis Alberto Sánchez\' personal correspondence with APRA leaders such as Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre, Manuel Seoane, and Nicanor Mujica is located in the <title>Correspondence</title> series. This series documents official APRA party activities, official communication to APRA party members abroad or in exile, and the dispute between Luis Alberto Sánchez and Apristas in Guatemala leading to disciplinary hearings against Sánchez. The majority of the correspondence in this series was annotated and summarized in <title>Literature and Politics in Latin America: An Annotated Calendar of the Luis Alberto Sanchez Correspondence, 1919-1980</title>.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"da18934671eef31ef1b6619b9695943c\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_62a4354bdecc383f32473e6f590fb95c\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:26:53','2022-04-09 23:26:53','2022-04-09 23:26:53',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(892,1,NULL,4540,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The <title>Correspondence</title> series, 1919-1991 (Bulk 1930-1969) (5.34 linear feet) consists of personal correspondence received, written, and collected by Luis Alberto Sánchez. This series is arranged in alphabetical order by name followed by chronological order. The majority of the correspondence are letters received by Luis Alberto Sánchez with a smaller number of letters written by Luis Alberto Sánchez. A very small number of items are letters written by correspondents to others and collected by Dr. Sánchez. These are retained in this series to reflect the original arrangement imposed by Don Henderson in consultation with Luis Alberto Sánchez. This series demonstrates Dr. Sánchez\' relationships with APRA leadership and APRA members such as Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre, Manuel Seoane, Nicanor Mujica, and Armando Villanueva del Campo. It also demonstrates Dr. Sánchez\' relationships with the Peruvian government, foreign governments, and other prominent political figures throughout Latin America such as Juan José Arévalo, Fernando Belaúnde Terry, Rómulo Betancourt, and Juan Bosch. This series also demonstrates Dr. Sánchez\' relationships with Latin American literary figures such as Alfredo González Prada, Alfonso Hernández Catá, José Carlos Mariátegui, Gabriela Mistral, Pablo Neruda, and César Vallejo as well as publishers in Peru and internationally. \\n\\nResearchers should note that much of the correspondence with Apristas and other Latin American political figures is written under pseudonyms. After transferring his papers to Penn State University, Luis Alberto Sánchez worked directly with Don Henderson and Grace Pérez to properly identify these correspondents. The majority of the correspondence in this series was annotated and summarized in <title>Literature and Politics in Latin America: An Annotated Calendar of the Luis Alberto Sanchez Correspondence, 1919-1980</title> and that the majority of the correspondence has been microfilmed. However, Pennsylvania State University received some of the correspondence after the book\'s publication and microfilming. Researchers should note that some folders include explanatory notes written by Luis Alberto Sánchez. In addition, during his 1974 visit, Luis Alberto Sánchez discussed three letters in a recording located in the <title>Pennsylvania State University</title> series.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"3b7c3865f6f46a9b253dd15764680f0c\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_1f4f6eb7d2b602422cd9e70a8a6e1563\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:26:53','2022-04-09 23:26:54','2022-04-09 23:26:53',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(893,1,NULL,4541,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The <title>Manuscripts and Publications</title> series, 1925-1992 (Bulk 1960-1979) (5.75 linear feet) consists of written and typed manuscripts as well as copies of printed publications written by Dr. Sánchez. This series is arranged chiefly by <title>Cuaderno de Bitácora</title> articles in numerical index order (a copy of this index is included in the collection folder and is available on request). The remaining publications had no original order and no order was imposed other than to house and inventory the materials. This series chiefly consists of articles written for the <title>Cuaderno de Bitácora</title> and similar publications. Of note are writings about politics, Latin American literature, and articles eulogizing figures such as José María Arguedas and Oswaldo Hercelles García. Researchers should note that many folders include brief notes about the contents and people and themes represented in each <title>Cuaderno de Bitácora</title> article.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"2dfd27848718f8fcec204480b2c3c271\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_3480a73fe93b378760f9af6959d5ec92\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:26:54','2022-04-09 23:26:54','2022-04-09 23:26:54',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(895,1,NULL,4543,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The <title>Collected Material</title> series, 1691-1989 (Bulk 1917-1979) (1 linear feet) includes various types of material collected by Dr. Sánchez, including poetry, clippings, biographical materials, and Peruvian political ephemera such as leaflets and pamphlets. The political leaflets and pamphlets are arranged chronologically while the remainder of the series is arranged alphabetically. The political materials include government propaganda, leaflets for elections, and copies of government documents.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"dd9398a3ddeef54c9aa489f55d4ca95d\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_3b0d1a221d7ffeb61f1b71e19957c7ae\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:26:54','2022-04-09 23:26:54','2022-04-09 23:26:54',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(896,1,NULL,4544,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The <title>Pennsylvania State University</title> series, 1960-1994 (0.75 linear feet) includes material collected by Pennsylvania State University about Luis Alberto Sánchez and this collection. The majority of this series consists of the original correspondence between Pennsylvania Staff University, Luis Alberto Sánchez, and intermediaries about the collection. While normally this material would be separated to the Collection Folder, this correspondence demonstrates the long term relationship between Dr. Sánchez and the University as well as Dr. Sánchez\' collaboration with Don Henderson to curate his papers. Since this correspondence was interfiled into the collection in the early 1990s, has been open and available to researchers, and provides an interesting insight into the collection\'s custodian and curatorial history, this correspondence is retained in the collection. In addition to correspondence, this series includes a list of books owned by Luis Alberto Sánchez, clippings, an audio recording of Luis Alberto Sánchez discussing his correspondence, and <title>Cuadero de Bitácora</title> articles collected by University librarians (and not transferred by Dr. Sánchez). This series also includes the master microfilm reels of the correspondence and <title>Cuaderno de Bitácora</title>. Master microfilm reels are only open to Special Collections staff, but access copies are available in the <title>Microforms and Government Information Library</title>.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"b303613684a94ecb764b383d993b51f3\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_9baabfbf097b0b133a4a6eb2f9d7f600\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:26:54','2022-04-09 23:26:54','2022-04-09 23:26:54',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(897,1,NULL,4560,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Signed by Luis Alberto Sánchez, Manuel Seoane, Magda Portal, Luis Lopez Aliaya, Carlos Alberto Izaguirre, and Guillermo Diaz Lira\",\"subnote_guid\":\"bb59d3fe6fe5838ee8ae5513fb988dca\"}],\"type\":\"odd\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_dfad49a69845f02622aa7e75b681b935\",\"label\":\"General\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:26:56','2022-04-09 23:26:56','2022-04-09 23:26:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(899,1,NULL,4574,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Includes message from Haya de la Torre to Franklin D. Roosevelt\",\"subnote_guid\":\"9179bf27ea33fce9c0c15e4f9c2989ad\"}],\"type\":\"odd\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_e38e5f0385ed19f1bcc12ee4bcb31014\",\"label\":\"General\"}','admin','admin','2022-04-09 23:26:59','2022-04-09 23:26:59','2022-04-09 23:26:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL